---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Study Hub"
  description="Draft terms for using the Study Hub website and learning resources."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Draft for review</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p>These draft terms describe basic expectations for using Study Hub. They should be reviewed before being treated as a formal legal policy.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>Using Study Hub</h2>
        <p>Study Hub provides learning materials and tools for personal, educational use. Use the site lawfully and do not interfere with its operation, attempt unauthorized access, or misuse its forms and services.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Learning materials</h2>
        <p>Materials are provided to support study and revision. Curricula, exam requirements, and resource availability can change; confirm important academic requirements with your school and the relevant education authorities.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Contributions and suggestions</h2>
        <p>Do not submit private, sensitive, unlawful, or identifying information through public contribution areas. Suggestions may be reviewed before publication. Do not submit material that you do not have permission to share.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>External resources</h2>
        <p>Study Hub may link to external websites and resources. Those destinations are operated independently and may have their own terms and policies.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For questions about these draft terms, contact <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com">Study Hub</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>